verifyReason:
Kit.screen clamps the scale to ≥0.55, and these controllers add no touch compensation. Results at 0.55:
- toast text: TextScaled with UITextSizeConstraint 20..11 in a 236x46 box, which works out to about 9-11 real px for typical 2-line messages and 6 px at the floor (the 6 px figure is the worst case, not typical);
- feed: 17 → 9.4 px;
- EventsHUD pills: 20 → 11 px;
- Hot Drop info and distance: 18/16 → 9.9/8.8 px;
- DrivingUI car name: 17 → 9.4 px.
HUDController's touch cells, MenuController.windowScale and TutorialController's TOUCH_CARD_SCALE do compensate, so the gap is inconsistent across controllers.

